    "putt-water": {
      "_bug": "PARTIALLY FIXED, and the original diagnosis was wrong. 187,010 -> 94,110. The note here used to blame makeWaterPlane's ydPerSegment (0.12, which saturated its 160-segment clamp on both axes). That was real but MINOR: raising it to 0.6 saved 41,900. Ablating the scene in the harness found the bulk elsewhere -- water.ts makeWetBankRect computed seg = max(w, d) / 0.35 and applied it to BOTH axes, so the 30x56 tide pool got the long side's 170 segments across its 32-unit short side: 170x170 quads = 57,800 triangles, submitted twice = 115,600, four fifths of this scene. Fixed per-axis (same intended 0.35 density, now actually applied), saving another 51,000. WHAT REMAINS, ~64,600, is a SHAPE problem, not a density one: the overlay is a full plane that tessellates a 30x56 interior at uniform alpha in order to draw a 1.1-unit band around its border. The fix is a border RING, which changes shared water geometry and needs its own visual gate. Until then this ceiling is a baseline, NOT approval -- 94k is still 9x every other putt scene, on the board that should be the cheapest thing golf ships.",
